            "description": "Watch Hamburger SV vs SC Freiburg highlights and goals from Bundesliga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on May 10, 2026. The Bundesliga clash on 2026-05-10 between Hamburger SV and SC Freiburg lived up to every bit of the pre-match hype. In front of a raucous crowd of 57,274 fans, the two sides engaged in a tactical and physical battle that kept everyone on the edge of their seats until the final whistle. Early Exchange of Blows The game exploded into life in the 14th minute when Bakery Jatta found the back of the net for Hamburger SV . Assisted by Albert Groenbaek , Jatta showed great composure to fire home with his right foot. However, the celebrations were short-lived. Just two minutes later, SC Freiburg responded with clinical precision following a defensive lapse by Bruno Ogbus . Lukas Kuebler delivered a cross that found Igor Matanovic , who executed a stunning right-footed volley to level the score at 1-1. The intensity remained high throughout the first half, with Kuebler picking up a yellow card for a dangerous challenge as both teams fought for control of the midfield. Second Half Momentum Shift The match took a decisive turn midway through the second half. In the 64th minute, a mistake by goalkeeper Noah Atubolu proved costly for the visitors. Luka Vuskovic capitalized on the error, seeing his right-footed shot deflected into the net to restore the lead for Hamburger SV . Vuskovic was booked for his exuberant celebrations, but the home side wasn't finished. Only three minutes later, Nicolai Remberg set up Fabio Balde , who calmly slotted the ball home to make it 3-1, putting Hamburg firmly in the driving seat. A Frantic Finale SC Freiburg refused to go down without a fight and mounted a late charge. In the 87th minute, Vincenzo Grifo whipped in a cross from a corner that Igor Matanovic headed home for his second goal of the match, setting up a nervy finish. The closing moments were pure drama; Hamburger SV 's Fabio Vieira struck the post with a brilliant long-range effort, and Rayan Philippe missed a golden opportunity to extend the lead during stoppage time. Despite the intense pressure and a late flurry of yellow cards for Nicolas Capaldo and Lucas Hoeler , Hamburg managed to hold on for a vital victory."
