            "description": "Watch Eintracht Frankfurt vs Hamburger SV highlights and goals from Bundesliga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on May 2, 2026. Eintracht Frankfurt vs. Borussia Dortmund: A Bundesliga Clash of Goals and Momentum Swings Borussia Dortmund secured a vital victory over Eintracht Frankfurt in a thrilling Bundesliga encounter on May 2, 2026. The match, played out on a vibrant pitch, was a see-saw battle that kept fans on the edge of their seats until the final whistle. Frankfurt's Early Momentum Eintracht Frankfurt set the early tone for the game, finding the back of the net just 2 minutes in. A key pass from Mahmoud Dahoud set up Can Uzun , who finished with his right foot to give the hosts an early lead and spark optimism among the home faithful. Dortmund's Swift Response The Eagles' lead, however, proved to be short-lived. Borussia Dortmund demonstrated resilience and drew level in first-half stoppage time. At 45+1 minutes, following an assist from Maximilian Beier , Nico Schlotterbeck scored with his left foot, ensuring the scores were level heading into the break. A Second Half of Intense Goalscoring The second half saw Borussia Dortmund take the lead. At 42 minutes, a decisive pass from Julian Ryerson found Serhou Guirassy , who finished with his right foot to turn the game on its head and put the visitors in front. The Black and Yellow's momentum continued, and at the 72nd minute, the team extended their advantage. A well-worked move saw Jobe Bellingham play the crucial pass to Maximilian Beier , who then teed up Samuele Inacio . The player slotted home with his right foot, pushing Borussia Dortmund 's lead to 3-1 and seemingly putting them on course for victory. Frankfurt's Late Fightback Eintracht Frankfurt refused to give up. In the closing stages, the team pushed to narrow the deficit. At 87 minutes, in a display of persistence, Jonathan Burkardt found the net with his left foot, reigniting hopes of a comeback and making the scoreline 3-2. Stoppage-Time Drama As the game entered stoppage time, the tension was palpable. Borussia Dortmund saw Samuele Inacio receive a yellow card for time-wasting at 90+1 minutes, followed by Gregor Kobel at 90+4 minutes, in a bid to hold onto their lead. Despite Eintracht Frankfurt 's efforts to find an equalizer, Borussia Dortmund managed to maintain their advantage until the final whistle, securing a hard-fought three points. Ball possession at the end of the match slightly favoured Borussia Dortmund with 56% to Eintracht Frankfurt 's 44%, but the intensity and scoreline fluctuations defined this exciting Bundesliga fixture."
